{"title": "Step-by-step: understand credits and pricing without Photoshop (ReWords AI)", "subject": "Step-by-step: understand credits and pricing without Photoshop (ReWords AI)", "body": "# Step-by-step: understand credits and pricing without Photoshop (ReWords AI)\n\nNeed to understand credits and pricing but don't have the original design file or Photoshop skills? This guide explains how to do it with [ReWords AI](https://rewordsai.app/), a free online tool whose one-line pitch is simple: edit the text inside any image online, for free. If you want to jump straight in, start here: [credit packs and monthly plans for ReWords AI](https://rewordsai.app/pricing).\n\n## What ReWords AI does\n\nReWords AI uses credits: you get free trial credits after sign-in with no credit card, and per-edit cost scales with output resolution. It works on screenshots, posters, memes, YouTube thumbnails, flyers, and product packaging shots.\n\n## Key features\n\n- Browser-based: nothing to install; it works online, no Photoshop skills needed.\n- Free to start: trial credits after sign-in, no credit card required.\n- Edit text: select any text in a PNG, JPG, or WebP image and type a replacement.\n- Style matching: the AI makes a best-effort match of the original font, color, and background.\n- Translate text: translate text in images, with free translation suggestions (fair use).\n- Remove text: leave the replacement blank to cleanly erase the selected words.\n\n## When it is useful\n\nTypical situations where editing text directly in the image saves time:\n\n- Memes whose caption you want to rewrite\n- Screenshots for documentation, tutorials, and slide decks\n- Posters and flyers that need a new date, venue, or offer\n- YouTube thumbnails when you want to test a different title\n- Manga or comic pages you want to translate\n\n## How to understand credits and pricing: step by step\n\n1. Open ReWords AI in your browser and sign in to receive free trial credits.\n2. Upload your image (PNG, JPG, or WebP).\n3. Click or select the text you want to change.\n4. Type the new words \u2014 or leave the field empty to remove the text.\n5. Let the AI render the edit, matching font, color, and background as closely as it can.\n6. Check the result, then download the edited image.\n\n### Tips for better results\n\n- Keep replacement text roughly the same length as the original so it fits the space naturally.\n- Use the highest-quality source image you have; cleaner pixels give the AI more to work with.\n- For translations, review the suggested wording before rendering the final image.\n- Edit one text block at a time when an image contains several lines in different styles.\n\n## Pricing in short\n\nSign in for free trial credits \u2014 no credit card. Credit packs start at $5.99 for 100 credits and monthly plans at $9.99 for 420 credits. An edit costs 10, 20, or 30 credits for 1K, 2K, or 4K output; translation suggestions are free (fair use).\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is ReWords AI free?\n\nYou get free trial credits after sign-in, with no credit card needed. For heavier use there are credit packs (from $5.99 for 100 credits) and monthly plans (from $9.99 for 420 credits).\n\n### How many credits does an edit cost?\n\nIt scales with resolution: 1K = 10 credits, 2K = 20 credits, 4K = 30 credits. Translation suggestions are free under fair use.\n\n### What should I not use it for?\n\nDo not use it to edit IDs, receipts, or official documents.\n\n### Which file formats are supported?\n\nPNG, JPG, and WebP images.\n\n### Is it a replacement for Photoshop?\n\nNo. ReWords AI is a focused online tool for text inside images, not a full photo editor, and it is not an offline/desktop app.\n\n## Summary\n\nReWords AI is a lightweight, browser-based way to edit, replace, remove, or translate text in images while keeping the original look. It is great for creators, marketers, and e-commerce sellers. Try it at [ReWords AI](https://rewordsai.app/).\n\n", "content": "# Step-by-step: understand credits and pricing without Photoshop (ReWords AI)\n\nNeed to understand credits and pricing but don't have the original design file or Photoshop skills? This guide explains how to do it with [ReWords AI](https://rewordsai.app/), a free online tool whose one-line pitch is simple: edit the text inside any image online, for free. If you want to jump straight in, start here: [credit packs and monthly plans for ReWords AI](https://rewordsai.app/pricing).\n\n## What ReWords AI does\n\nReWords AI uses credits: you get free trial credits after sign-in with no credit card, and per-edit cost scales with output resolution. It works on screenshots, posters, memes, YouTube thumbnails, flyers, and product packaging shots.\n\n## Key features\n\n- Browser-based: nothing to install; it works online, no Photoshop skills needed.\n- Free to start: trial credits after sign-in, no credit card required.\n- Edit text: select any text in a PNG, JPG, or WebP image and type a replacement.\n- Style matching: the AI makes a best-effort match of the original font, color, and background.\n- Translate text: translate text in images, with free translation suggestions (fair use).\n- Remove text: leave the replacement blank to cleanly erase the selected words.\n\n## When it is useful\n\nTypical situations where editing text directly in the image saves time:\n\n- Memes whose caption you want to rewrite\n- Screenshots for documentation, tutorials, and slide decks\n- Posters and flyers that need a new date, venue, or offer\n- YouTube thumbnails when you want to test a different title\n- Manga or comic pages you want to translate\n\n## How to understand credits and pricing: step by step\n\n1. Open ReWords AI in your browser and sign in to receive free trial credits.\n2. Upload your image (PNG, JPG, or WebP).\n3. Click or select the text you want to change.\n4. Type the new words \u2014 or leave the field empty to remove the text.\n5. Let the AI render the edit, matching font, color, and background as closely as it can.\n6. Check the result, then download the edited image.\n\n### Tips for better results\n\n- Keep replacement text roughly the same length as the original so it fits the space naturally.\n- Use the highest-quality source image you have; cleaner pixels give the AI more to work with.\n- For translations, review the suggested wording before rendering the final image.\n- Edit one text block at a time when an image contains several lines in different styles.\n\n## Pricing in short\n\nSign in for free trial credits \u2014 no credit card. Credit packs start at $5.99 for 100 credits and monthly plans at $9.99 for 420 credits. An edit costs 10, 20, or 30 credits for 1K, 2K, or 4K output; translation suggestions are free (fair use).\n\n## FAQ\n\n### Is ReWords AI free?\n\nYou get free trial credits after sign-in, with no credit card needed. For heavier use there are credit packs (from $5.99 for 100 credits) and monthly plans (from $9.99 for 420 credits).\n\n### How many credits does an edit cost?\n\nIt scales with resolution: 1K = 10 credits, 2K = 20 credits, 4K = 30 credits. Translation suggestions are free under fair use.\n\n### What should I not use it for?\n\nDo not use it to edit IDs, receipts, or official documents.\n\n### Which file formats are supported?\n\nPNG, JPG, and WebP images.\n\n### Is it a replacement for Photoshop?\n\nNo. ReWords AI is a focused online tool for text inside images, not a full photo editor, and it is not an offline/desktop app.\n\n## Summary\n\nReWords AI is a lightweight, browser-based way to edit, replace, remove, or translate text in images while keeping the original look. It is great for creators, marketers, and e-commerce sellers. Try it at [ReWords AI](https://rewordsai.app/).\n\n", "text": "# Step-by-step: understand credits and pricing without Photoshop (ReWords AI)\n\nNeed to understand credits and pricing but don't have the original design file or Photoshop skills? This guide explains how to do it with [ReWords